 *   line, the guide for where to stand. "I'm on the spot" opens the session
 *   and goes on to Fire rate; the spot's own wall (box, brightness, the ammo
 *   counter's place) and field of view go with the wall step.
 *   D419 (owner, 2026-10-20): ONE Automatic. A game with NO trained spot is
 *   not told so and offered a choice: the same flow says to go to any flat
 *   wall with some detail (method 'auto', recoil-wall.js's anywhere) and the
 *   Core reads the view there.
 *
 *   C. THE SENSITIVITY CHECK (anywhere only, on the Fire rate page, once per
 *      game and config): POST /recoil/auto {"op":"arm","sens":true} then GO;
 *      the player's controls are paused (as Measure fire rate), the Core aims
 *      down sights and moves the aim by known counts through the Script's own
 *      door, the view measured anywhere; the answer (counts per frame width
 *      and height) is kept per config and per game (recoil-wall.js setSens)
 *      and makes the Script's 100% the real size.
 *
