 * customer's): the owner stands on the spot, the Core shows how much of the
 * view it can recognise, "Capture this view" keeps the Core's own 48 x 27
 * thumbnail (the reference) and a picture for players, then the owner fires
 * a test magazine at the wall (the Core watches, as a player's would), checks
 * the traced line, and saves the spot with the wall the Core found (its box
 * grown a little, its brightness) and the field of view: kept on this device
 * to try at once, and downloaded as a spot file and a picture, which
 * dashboard/tools/add-recoil-spot.js writes into the game pack
 * (docs/HOW-TO-TRAIN-A-SPOT.md). Real frames only.
 *
 * NOTHING HERE STORES A PICTURE ON THE CORE: the reference thumbnail lives
 * for the session; the spot's picture is an app file (game-packs/spots/).
 *
